This is not completely true. The only use I've ever made of this command,
is the following:
You dip a dart or an arrow into a potion. (Don't forget the potions name)
Then you check if the potion is still in your inventory. If it isn't, it
is a potion of posion and your dart or arrow has been enchanted!!!!!
Next time you come across this potion, call it a potion of poison and
enchant your arrows again.
If the potion is still in your inventory, nothing happened.

